cl builds an array of class objects by calling its own runtime helper, the vector constructor iterator ??_H@YAXPEAX_K1P6APEAX0@Z@Z, and passing it the element constructor; cxx1 emits the loop inline instead. So cl's object names a helper cxx1's does not. Neither is an ABI question - nothing outside the object can tell which was used - and cxx1 has no such helper to call, the runtime it links against being whatever the platform provides rather than a library of its own.
